      "side": 1,
      "message": "I get the ordering issue. I was a bit confusing by Rust documentation for start_thread_pool that says: \"This should be done before creating any Binder client or server.\"\nHowever this code will likely be valid:\n```\nfn main() {\n   let ctx \u003d createOurSdkContext(); // plan was to require threads here. We do create Binder clients here, but not yet use callbacks.\n\n   ...\n\n   startThreadPool(1); // optional in this example\n   joinThreadPool(); // this call on itself will not mark the pool as started, even though it will do the binder event processing.\n}\n```\n\nIIUC `getThreadPoolMaxTotalThreadCount` is not exposet in https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/native/libs/binder/ndk/include_platform/android/binder_process.h and it would mean NDK API change to add it.\nAnd given we are based on A16, likely it is not feasible to make it.\n\nIn that case we will likely have to document that as an requirment for users to handle threads by hand. Hopefully in most cases we have a zygote-style initialization for most of our services and only a very low level",
